# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend/.env.defaults holds the MongoDB connection secret, so it is IGNORED
# and must NOT be committed. It is still baked into the Docker image at build
# time (it is not listed in .dockerignore), so keep the file on disk to deploy.
#
# To recreate it, create backend/.env.defaults containing a single line:
#
#   MONGO_URL=mongodb+srv://<User>:<Password>@<cluster-host>/?retryWrites=true&w=majority&appName=<AppName>
#
# Get the real <User>, <Password>, <cluster-host> and <AppName> from the
# MongoDB Atlas console: Database > Connect > Drivers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backend/.env.defaults

